meta {
  name: Update Patient
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/patients/{{patientId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "city": "Mysuru",
    "bloodGroup": "A_POS",
    "patientCategory": "VIP",
    "ptCategoryId": "{{ptCategoryId}}",
    "maritalStatus": "MARRIED",
    "status": "CREATED",
    "isActive": false,
    "alternateMobileNumber": "+919822222222",
    "photoUrl": "https://s3-ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/stage.ez.reports/uploads/finance-attachments/{{tenantId}}/patient-photos/updated-photo.jpg"
  }
}

docs {
  Update a patient's details (scoped to the caller's tenant). Every field is
  optional — send only what changes; same field rules as **Create Patient**.
  This includes `status` (`DRAFT`/`CREATED`) — e.g. promote a `DRAFT` patient to
  `CREATED`, and `ptCategoryId` (a Registration Settings PT Category, validated
  against the active branch; `null` clears it; the patient's current category
  sent back unchanged is accepted without re-validation). Medical-history
  records are managed via their own nested endpoints, NOT here.

  **Branch rule:** patients are editable tenant-wide, but the per-branch
  `ptCategoryId` is owned by the patient's registration branch. A caller whose
  active branch differs from the patient's `branchId` can edit every other field,
  but any `ptCategoryId` they send is silently ignored (the patient keeps its
  current category) — no 403. Tenant-level profiles (no active branch), the
  patient's own branch, and patients with no registration branch may change the
  category too. (Deletes remain restricted to the registration branch — see
  **Delete Patient**.)

  `tenantId`/`branchId` are never accepted. A duplicate active `mobile` in the
  tenant → 409 `PATIENT_MOBILE_CONFLICT`. 404 `PATIENT_NOT_FOUND` if
  missing/other tenant.
}
